mainmenu "PhysDAQ Hub"

source "Kconfig.zephyr"

menu "PhysDAQ Hub"

config PHYSDAQ_PPG_ODR_HZ
	int "PPG sample rate per sensor (Hz)"
	default 100
	help
	  Sample rate programmed into both MAX30102 SPO2_CONFIG registers, and
	  recorded in the log file header so older samples in each FIFO burst
	  can be back-dated offline (see src/storage.h).

	  Only 50, 100, 200 and 400 are accepted. Those are the rates the part
	  permits in SpO2 mode at the 411 us / 18-bit pulse width this firmware
	  uses; other values are rejected at build time. 100 is the rate the
	  single-PPG firmware was validated at — treat anything higher as
	  unproven until a long run confirms the FIFOs keep up.

config PHYSDAQ_SD_SYNC_INTERVAL_MS
	int "Interval between forced filesystem syncs (ms)"
	default 1000
	range 100 10000
	help
	  Upper bound on how much data an ungraceful power loss can cost. The
	  storage thread calls fs_sync() at least this often, so at the default
	  1000 ms and 2 sensors at 100 Hz, a hard power cut loses at most one
	  second of acquisition (~200 samples, 3.2 kB).

	  Lowering this shrinks the loss window but costs an SD FAT+dirent
	  write each time, which is the operation most likely to stall the card
	  for tens of milliseconds.

config PHYSDAQ_DEEP_SLEEP
	bool "Enter deep sleep after an idle timeout"
	default n
	help
	  Single-PPG node behaviour: after PHYSDAQ_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SEC without
	  motion, skin contact or a BLE link, shut the sensors down and enter
	  System Off (~0.4 uA), waking on the IMU activity interrupt.

	  Off by default on the hub. A hub records unattended to microSD and is
	  routinely stationary and unworn on a bench, which is exactly the state
	  the idle timer treats as "put down" — it would power the node off
	  mid-session. Idle accounting still runs and is still reported on the
	  status line when this is disabled; only the System Off is suppressed.

config PHYSDAQ_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SEC
	int "Seconds of inactivity before deep sleep"
	default 10
	range 5 300
	help
	  Only acts when PHYSDAQ_DEEP_SLEEP is enabled. Counts consecutive
	  seconds without gyroscope motion, without IR contact (src/contact.c)
	  and without a BLE link — worn but still (e.g. resting) does not
	  trigger sleep, only set down and unworn does. Wake-up is the
	  LSM6DS3TR-C activity interrupt on INT1.

endmenu
